#+LATEX_CLASS: article-hebrew
* Rich Footnotes System

Full document capability inside footnotes: unlimited headings, lists, tables (with merging), nested footnotes, code blocks, description lists.

** Packages

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package ox-pandoc
  :after org
  :config
  (setq org-pandoc-options '((standalone . t)))
  (setq org-pandoc-options-for-latex-pdf '((pdf-engine . \"lualatex\"))))
#+end_src

** Documentation

*** Overview

This system provides rich content inside footnotes for:
- LaTeX (bigfoot + custom environments)
- Typst (native + helpers)
- ConTeXt (native + helpers)  
- Org-mode (preprocessor auto-converts on export)
- Pandoc (PDF, DOCX, HTML via ox-pandoc)

All support:
- 20 levels of headings
- 20 levels of nested lists (itemize, enumerate, description)
- Tables with colspan/rowspan, captions, numbering
- Code blocks
- Nested footnotes (10 levels)

*** Quick Reference

| System  | Rich Footnote Command/Block                    |
|---------+------------------------------------------------|
| LaTeX   | =\\rfn{...}= or =\\rfnB{...}= etc.               |
| Typst   | =#rfn[...]= or native =#footnote[...]=         |
| ConTeXt | =\\startRFN= ... =\\stopRFN=                     |
| Org     | Auto-detected, or =#+BEGIN_RICHFN id= block    |

*** LaTeX Usage

**** Simple rich footnote:
#+begin_example latex
\\rfn{
  \\fnh{1}{Main Heading}
  
  \\begin{fnitemize}
    \\item First item
    \\begin{fnitemize}
      \\item Nested item
    \\end{fnitemize}
  \\end{fnitemize}
  
  \\begin{fntab}{|l|l|}{Table Caption}
    \\hline
    A & B \\\\
    \\hline
    \\multicolumn{2}{|c|}{Merged} \\\\
    \\hline
  \\end{fntab}
  
  \\begin{fncode}{python}
  def hello():
      print(\"Hello\")
  \\end{fncode}
}
#+end_example

**** Nested footnotes:
#+begin_example latex
\\rfn{
  Main content\\rfnmark{B}.
  \\rfntext{B}{
    Second level\\rfnmark{C}.
    \\rfntext{C}{Third level.}
  }
}
#+end_example

**** Heading levels (1-20):
=\\fnh{1}{...}= through =\\fnh{20}{...}=

**** List types:
- =\\begin{fnitemize}= ... =\\end{fnitemize}= (bullets)
- =\\begin{fnenumerate}= ... =\\end{fnenumerate}= (numbered)
- =\\begin{fndescription}= ... =\\end{fndescription}= (description)

*** Typst Usage

#+begin_example typst
#rfn[
  #fnh(1)[Main Heading]
  
  - List item 1
    - Nested item
  
  #fn-table(
    caption: \"My Table\",
    columns: 2,
    [A], [B],
    table.cell(colspan: 2)[Merged],
  )
  
  #fn-code(\"python\", `
  def hello():
      print(\"Hello\")
  `)
  
  #rfn[Nested footnote]
]
#+end_example

*** ConTeXt Usage

#+begin_example context
\\startRFN
\\fnh[1]{Main Heading}

\\startfnitemize
\\item First item
\\startfnitemize
\\item Nested
\\stopfnitemize
\\stopfnitemize

\\startfntable[caption={My Table}]
\\NC A \\NC B \\NC\\NR
\\NC \\use{2}{Merged} \\NC\\NR
\\stopfntable

\\startfncode[python]
def hello():
    print(\"Hello\")
\\stopfncode

\\startRFN
Nested footnote
\\stopRFN
\\stopRFN
#+end_example

*** Org Usage

**** Automatic detection:
Just write org syntax in footnote definitions:

#+begin_example org
Text with footnote[fn:1].

[fn:1] 
* Heading in Footnote

- List item 1
  - Nested item
- List item 2

| Col A | Col B |
|-------+-------|
| 1     | 2     |

#+begin_src python
def hello():
    print(\"Hello\")
#+end_src

Another footnote reference[fn:2].

[fn:2] Nested footnote content.
#+end_example

**** Explicit block (for complex cases):

#+begin_example org
#+BEGIN_RICHFN myid
* Heading

- List

| Table |

#+BEGIN_RICHFN nested1
Nested footnote
#+END_RICHFN

#+END_RICHFN

Reference with [fn:myid] in text.
#+end_example

** LaTeX Preamble

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defvar my/latex-rich-footnotes-preamble
  \"% ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
% RICH FOOTNOTES SYSTEM - Full document capability in footnotes
% ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

% ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
% NESTED FOOTNOTES (10 levels: default, B-J)
% ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\\\\usepackage{bigfoot}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{default}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{B}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{C}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{D}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{E}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{F}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{G}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{H}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{I}
\\\\DeclareNewFootnote{J}

% Shortcuts
\\\\newcommand{\\\\rfn}[1]{\\\\footnote{#1}}
\\\\newcommand{\\\\rfnB}[1]{\\\\footnoteB{#1}}
\\\\newcommand{\\\\rfnC}[1]{\\\\footnoteC{#1}}
