** Mode-Specific Keybindings

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
;; LaTeX mode
(with-eval-after-load 'latex
  (define-key LaTeX-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f\") #'hydra-rich-footnotes/body)
  (define-key LaTeX-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f r\") #'my/insert-rich-footnote-latex)
  (define-key LaTeX-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f n\") #'my/insert-nested-rich-footnote-latex))

;; Typst mode
(with-eval-after-load 'typst-ts-mode
  (when (boundp 'typst-ts-mode-map)
    (define-key typst-ts-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f\") #'hydra-rich-footnotes/body)
    (define-key typst-ts-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f r\") #'my/insert-rich-footnote-typst)))

;; Org mode
(with-eval-after-load 'org
  (define-key org-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f\") #'hydra-rich-footnotes/body)
  (define-key org-mode-map (kbd \"C-c f r\") #'my/insert-rich-footnote-org))
#+end_src" "* Rich Footnotes System

Full document capability inside footnotes: unlimited headings, lists, tables, nested footnotes.

** Documentation

*** Overview

This system provides rich content (headings, lists, tables) inside footnotes for:
- LaTeX (bigfoot + custom commands)
- Typst (native support)
- ConTeXt (native support)
- Org-mode (preprocessor converts to export format)
- Pandoc (via ox-pandoc)

*** Usage Quick Reference

| System  | Simple Footnote      | Rich Footnote                    |
|---------+----------------------+----------------------------------|
| LaTeX   | =\\footnote{}=        | =\\rfootnote{}= or =\\footnoteB{}= |
| Typst   | =#footnote[]=        | =#footnote[...rich content...]=  |
| ConTeXt | =\\footnote{}=        | =\\startfootnote= ... =\\stopfootnote= |
| Org     | =[fn:1]=             | Auto-detected or =#+BEGIN_RICHFN= |

*** LaTeX Rich Footnotes

Basic (level 1):
#+begin_example
\\rfootnote{
  \\fnheading{Title}
  \\begin{fnlist}
    \\item First
    \\item Second
  \\end{fnlist}
  \\begin{fntable}{|c|c|}
    \\hline
    A & B \\\\
    \\hline
  \\end{fntable}
}
#+end_example

Nested (level 2+):
#+begin_example
\\rfootnote{
  Text\\rfootnotemark[B].
  \\rfootnotetext[B]{
    Nested content with \\fnheading{Heading}
  }
}
#+end_example

Available levels: (none), B, C, D, E, F, G, H, I, J

*** Typst Rich Footnotes

#+begin_example
#footnote[
  = Heading Level 1
  == Heading Level 2
  
  - List item 1
    - Nested item
  - List item 2
  
  #table(
    columns: 2,
    [Header 1], [Header 2],
    [Cell 1], [Cell 2],
  )
  
  #footnote[Nested footnote]
]
#+end_example

*** ConTeXt Rich Footnotes

#+begin_example
\\startfootnote
\\subject{Heading}

\\startitemize
\\item First item
\\item Second item
\\stopitemize

\\starttabulate[|c|c|]
\\NC Header 1 \\NC Header 2 \\NC\\NR
\\NC Cell 1 \\NC Cell 2 \\NC\\NR
\\stoptabulate

\\startfootnote
Nested footnote
\\stopfootnote
\\stopfootnote
#+end_example

*** Org Rich Footnotes

**** Automatic Detection
Just write normal org syntax in footnote definitions:

#+begin_example
[fn:1] This footnote has rich content:

* Heading

- List item 1
- List item 2

| Col A | Col B |
|-------+-------|
| 1     | 2     |
#+end_example

The preprocessor auto-detects and converts on export.

**** Explicit Block (for complex cases)

#+begin_example
#+BEGIN_RICHFN 1
* Heading in Footnote

- Item with *bold*
- Item with /italic/

| Table | Here |
|-------+------|
| A     | B    |

#+BEGIN_RICHFN 2
Nested footnote content
#+END_RICHFN
#+END_RICHFN
#+end_example

