This configuration and documentation are released into the public domain. Use freely for Torah study, scholarship, and any other purpose." "#+TITLE: Emacs Configuration Guide
#+AUTHOR: Shaul
#+STARTUP: overview num
#+OPTIONS: toc:3

* Introduction

This is a comprehensive guide to a literate Emacs configuration optimized for:

- *Hebrew (RTL) as default*, with seamless switching to English (LTR)
- *Academic document preparation* with LaTeX (LuaLaTeX + Babel), ConTeXt, and Typst
- *Unlimited structure depth* in headings and lists (Org and LaTeX)
- *Nested footnotes* across all three document systems
- *Org-roam* for Zettelkasten-style note-taking with full Hebrew support
- *Seforim library management* for fast searching of large Hebrew text collections
- *PDF annotation* with org-noter integration
- *Bibliography management* with Citar

The configuration is written in literate Org format (=config.org=) and automatically tangles to =config.el= on save.

** System Requirements

This configuration runs on NixOS with a dedicated =emacs.nix= module. The following are provided by the NixOS configuration:

| Category | Packages |
|----------|----------|
| Emacs | =emacs-pgtk= (native Wayland, built-in =use-package=) |
| Nix-provided Emacs packages | =jinx=, =exec-path-from-shell=, =pdf-tools= (use =:ensure nil=) |
| TeX | =texlive.combined.scheme-full= (includes LuaLaTeX, ConTeXt) |
| Typst | =typst=, =tinymist= (LSP server) |
| Fonts | =culmus= (Hebrew: David CLM, Nachlieli CLM, Miriam Mono CLM), =jetbrains-mono=, =noto-fonts= |
| Search | =plocate=, =recoll=, =ripgrep=, =ripgrep-all=, =fd= |
| Spell | =enchant2=, =hunspell= with =en_US= and =he_IL= dictionaries |
| PDF | =poppler=, =poppler-utils= (for pdf-tools and recoll) |
| Document converters | =pandoc=, =antiword=, =catdoc=, =unzip=, =calibre= |
| Dev | =python3=, =python-lsp-server=, =rustc=, =cargo=, =rust-analyzer=, =jdk=, =jdt-language-server= |
| VCS | =git= |
| Other | =sqlite= (org-roam), =graphviz= (org-roam graph), =xapian= (recoll) |
| Icons | Run =M-x all-the-icons-install-fonts= after first launch |

*** NixOS Module

The Emacs environment is defined in =emacs.nix=. Import it from =configuration.nix=:

#+begin_example
imports = [ ./emacs.nix ];
#+end_example

The module provides:
- All system packages and fonts
- Emacs with Nix-provided packages (jinx, exec-path-from-shell, pdf-tools)
- Plocate service with hourly indexing
- Recoll configuration and systemd timer for periodic indexing
- User membership in =plocate= group
- Environment variables (=DICPATH=, =OSFONTDIR=)
- Seforim directory creation

*** Important: Nix-Provided vs MELPA Packages

Packages provided by Nix must use =:ensure nil= in =config.org=:

| Package | Source | =:ensure= |
|---------|--------|-----------|
| =jinx= | Nix | =nil= |
| =exec-path-from-shell= | Nix | =nil= |
| =pdf-tools= | Nix | =nil= |
| Everything else | MELPA | =t= (default) |

** File Locations

| File | Location |
|------|----------|
| NixOS Emacs module | =/etc/nixos/emacs.nix= (or your flake path) |
| Emacs config (source) | =~/.emacs.d/config.org= |
| Emacs config (tangled) | =~/.emacs.d/config.el= |
| Init file | =~/.emacs.d/init.el= |
| Org directory | =~/Documents/org/= |
| Org-roam notes | =~/Documents/roam/= |
| Roam daily notes | =~/Documents/roam/daily/= |
| Bibliography | =~/Documents/bibliography.bib= |
| Seforim library | =~/Documents/seforim/= |
| Undo history | =~/.emacs.d/undo-tree-history/= |
| Recoll config | =~/.recoll/recoll.conf= (managed by NixOS) |
| Plocate database | =/var/cache/locatedb= |

** First Run Tasks

After first launch:

1. Wait for MELPA packages to install (first startup is slow)

2. Install icon fonts:
   : M-x all-the-icons-install-fonts RET

3. Initialize org-roam database:
   : M-x org-roam-db-sync RET

4. Build Seforim indexes (if using Seforim library):
   : M-x seforim-reindex RET

5. Verify tools are available:
   : M-x seforim-status RET

Note: =pdf-tools= is installed via Nix and does not need =M-x pdf-tools-install=. It runs =pdf-tools-install :no-query= automatically.

** Verifying the Installation

After =sudo nixos-rebuild switch= and starting Emacs:

#+begin_src shell
# Verify plocate group membership (re-login after first rebuild)
groups | grep plocate

# Verify recoll config
cat ~/.recoll/recoll.conf

# Verify fonts
fc-list | grep -i \"david\\|nachlieli\\|miriam\"

# Verify tools
which plocate fd rg rga recoll typst tinymist lualatex
#+end_src

In Emacs:

#+begin_example
M-x jinx-languages RET        → should show \"en he\"
M-x seforim-status RET        → should show all tools ✓
C-h v exec-path RET           → should include /run/current-system/sw/bin
#+end_example

* Basic Emacs Usage

** Key Notation

| Notation | Meaning |
|----------|---------|
| =C-= | Hold Control key |
| =M-= | Hold Alt/Meta key |
| =S-= | Hold Shift key |
| =RET= | Press Enter |
| =SPC= | Press Space |
| =TAB= | Press Tab |

Example: =C-x C-f= means \"hold Control, press x, release, hold Control, press f\".

** Essential Commands

| Keybinding | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| =C-x C-f= | Open/create file |
| =C-x C-s= | Save file |
| =C-x C-c= | Quit Emacs |
| =C-x b= | Switch buffer (with consult) |
| =C-x C-b= | List buffers (ibuffer) |
| =C-x k= | Close buffer |
| =C-g= | Cancel current command |
| =M-x= | Run any command by name |
| =C-h k= | Describe what a keybinding does |
| =C-h f= | Describe a function |
| =C-h v= | Describe a variable |
| =C-h m= | Describe current mode |

** Navigation

| Keybinding | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| =C-f= / =C-b= | Forward/backward one character |
| =M-f= / =M-b= | Forward/backward one word |
| =C-n= / =C-p= | Next/previous line |
| =C-a= / =C-e= | Beginning/end of line |
| =M-<= / =M->= | Beginning/end of buffer |
| =C-v= / =M-v= | Page down/up |
| =C-s= | Search in buffer (consult-line) |
| =M-g g= | Go to line number |

** Editing

| Keybinding | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| =C-d= | Delete character forward |
| =M-d= | Delete word forward |
| =C-k= | Kill (cut) to end of line |
| =C-w= | Kill (cut) region |
| =M-w= | Copy region |
| =C-y= | Yank (paste) |
| =M-y= | Cycle through kill ring (after =C-y=) |
| =C-/= | Undo |
| =C-?= | Redo |
| =C-x u= | Visual undo tree |
| =C-SPC= | Set mark (start selection) |
| =C-x h= | Select entire buffer |

