#+AUTHOR: User
#+STARTUP: overview num
#+OPTIONS: toc:3

* Installation
** NixOS Configuration

1. Copy =emacs-packages.nix= to =/etc/nixos/=

2. Edit =/etc/nixos/configuration.nix= and add:

   #+begin_src nix
     imports = [
       ./hardware-configuration.nix
       ./emacs-packages.nix
     ];
   #+end_src

3. Rebuild:

   #+begin_src shell
     sudo nixos-rebuild switch
   #+end_src

** Emacs Configuration

1. Create directory:

   #+begin_src shell
     mkdir -p ~/.emacs.d
   #+end_src

2. Copy files:

   #+begin_src shell
     cp config.org ~/.emacs.d/
     cp init.el ~/.emacs.d/
   #+end_src

3. Create required directories:

   #+begin_src shell
     mkdir -p ~/Documents/roam
     mkdir -p ~/Documents/org
     touch ~/Documents/bibliography.bib
   #+end_src

4. Start Emacs and wait for packages to install

** First Run Tasks

After first launch:

1. Install icon fonts:
   : M-x all-the-icons-install-fonts RET

2. Initialize org-roam database:
   : M-x org-roam-db-sync RET

* Basic Emacs Usage
** Key Notation

| Notation | Meaning              |
|----------+----------------------|
| =C-=     | Hold Control key     |
| =M-=     | Hold Alt/Meta key    |
| =S-=     | Hold Shift key       |
| =RET=    | Press Enter          |
| =SPC=    | Press Space          |

** Essential Commands

| Keybinding  | Description              |
|-------------+--------------------------|
| =C-x C-f=   | Open/create file         |
| =C-x C-s=   | Save file                |
| =C-x C-c=   | Quit Emacs               |
| =C-x b=     | Switch buffer            |
| =C-x k=     | Close buffer             |
| =C-g=       | Cancel command           |
| =M-x=       | Run any command          |
| =C-h k=     | Describe keybinding      |
| =C-h f=     | Describe function        |
| =C-h v=     | Describe variable        |

** Navigation

| Keybinding      | Description               |
|-----------------+---------------------------|
| =C-f= / =C-b=   | Forward/backward char     |
| =M-f= / =M-b=   | Forward/backward word     |
| =C-n= / =C-p=   | Next/previous line        |
| =C-a= / =C-e=   | Beginning/end of line     |
| =M-<= / =M->=   | Beginning/end of buffer   |
| =C-v= / =M-v=   | Page down/up              |
| =C-s=           | Search (consult-line)     |
| =M-g g=         | Go to line number         |

** Editing

| Keybinding | Description               |
|------------+---------------------------|
| =C-d=      | Delete character          |
| =M-d=      | Delete word               |
| =C-k=      | Kill to end of line       |
| =C-w=      | Kill region (cut)         |
| =M-w=      | Copy region               |
| =C-y=      | Yank (paste)              |
| =M-y=      | Cycle kill ring           |
| =C-/=      | Undo                      |
| =C-?=      | Redo                      |
| =C-x u=    | Visual undo tree          |

** Windows

| Keybinding | Description                     |
|------------+---------------------------------|
| =C-x 2=    | Split horizontally (and follow) |
| =C-x 3=    | Split vertically (and follow)   |
| =C-x 0=    | Close current window            |
| =C-x 1=    | Close other windows             |
| =M-o=      | Switch window (ace-window)      |

** Focused Writing Mode

| Keybinding | Action                           |
|------------+----------------------------------|
| =C-c w=    | Toggle focused writing (80-col centered) |
| =C-c W=    | Set column width                 |

When enabled, text is soft-wrapped at 80 columns and visually centered in the window. No actual line breaks are inserted.

* Hebrew and RTL Support
** How Direction Works

The config automatically sets direction per major mode:

| Mode Type              | Default Direction |
|------------------------+-------------------|
| Org, LaTeX, text modes | RTL (Hebrew)      |
| Programming modes      | LTR (English)     |
| Other modes            | Auto-detect       |

You can always override manually with the keybindings below.

** Switching Languages

| Keybinding | Action                                 |
|------------+----------------------------------------|
| =F9=       | Toggle input method (Hebrew ↔ English) |
| =C-c d=    | Toggle text direction (RTL ↔ LTR)      |
| =C-c r=    | Force RTL direction                    |
| =C-c l=    | Force LTR direction                    |
| =C-c D=    | Direction controls menu (hydra)        |

** Visual Indicators

The modeline shows current state:
- =[RTL עב]= - Hebrew mode, right-to-left
- =[LTR EN]= - English mode, left-to-right

** Best Practices

1. *Hebrew documents*: Automatically RTL (Org, LaTeX, text modes)
2. *English documents*: Use =C-c l= for LTR, or it auto-detects
3. *Mixed documents*: Use =C-c d= to toggle as needed
4. *Code*: Automatically LTR (prog-mode)

** Spell Checking

Spell checking uses Flyspell with Hunspell. Switch between languages manually:

| Keybinding | Action                      |
|------------+-----------------------------|
| =C-c s e=  | Switch to English           |
| =C-c s h=  | Switch to Hebrew            |
| =M-$=      | Correct word at point       |
| =i=        | Add word to personal dict   |

When a correctly-spelled word is flagged (e.g., Hebrew word while in English mode), press =i= to add it to your personal dictionary (=~/.hunspell_personal=).

Spell checking is active in:
- All text/prose modes (Org, LaTeX, Markdown, etc.)
- Comments and strings in programming modes

* Document Systems Overview

This configuration supports three document systems:

| System    | Best For                          | Hebrew | Nested Footnotes          |
|-----------+-----------------------------------+--------+---------------------------|
| *LaTeX*   | Academic papers, journals         | ✓      | Separate blocks (bigfoot) |
| *ConTeXt* | Complex typography, books         | ✓      | Native local footnotes    |
| *Typst*   | Fast iteration, modern syntax     | ✓      | Sequential (with show rule) |

