** LSP (Eglot) Keybindings

| Keybinding | Action           |
|------------+------------------|
| =M-.=      | Go to definition |
| =M-,=      | Go back          |
| =M-?=      | Find references  |
| =C-c C-r=  | Rename symbol    |

** Running Code in Org

1. Create a code block:

#+begin_example
,#+begin_src python
print(\"Hello\")
,#+end_src
#+end_example

2. Place cursor in block
3. Press =C-c C-c= to execute
4. Results appear below

** Electric Pairs (Auto-closing Brackets)

Electric pairs (auto-inserting matching =()=, ={}=, =\"\"=, etc.) are enabled only in:
- Programming modes (Python, Rust, Java, etc.)
- LaTeX mode
- ConTeXt mode
- Typst mode
- Org source block editing (via =C-c '=)

They are *disabled* in prose modes (Org, Markdown, plain text) to avoid interfering with Hebrew writing.

* Version Control (Magit)
** Keybindings

| Keybinding | Action             |
|------------+--------------------|
| =C-x g=    | Magit status       |
| =C-x M-g=  | Magit dispatch     |
| =C-c g=    | Magit file dispatch|
| =C-c G=    | Git timemachine    |

** Basic Magit Workflow

1. Open status: =C-x g=
2. Stage changes: =s= on unstaged files
3. Commit: =c c=, write message, =C-c C-c=
4. Push: =P p=

* Undo and Redo

This config uses =undo-tree= for visual, persistent undo/redo:

| Keybinding | Action                                  |
|------------+-----------------------------------------|
| =C-/=      | Undo                                    |
| =C-?=      | Redo                                    |
| =C-x u=    | Visual undo tree (graphical view)       |

Undo history is saved between sessions in =~/.emacs.d/undo-tree-history/=.

In the visual undo tree:
- Use =p= / =n= to navigate up/down
- Use =b= / =f= to switch branches
- Press =q= to quit

* Adding New Packages
** Method 1: Edit config.org (Recommended)

1. Open =~/.emacs.d/config.org=

2. Find appropriate section or create new heading

3. Add a =use-package= block:

#+begin_example
,** My New Package

,#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package package-name
  :config
  ;; Configuration here
  )
,#+end_src
#+end_example

4. Save the file

5. Either:
   - Restart Emacs, OR
   - Place cursor in the block and press =C-c C-c= to evaluate

** Method 2: Quick Install (Temporary)

1. =M-x package-install RET=
2. Type package name
3. Press =RET=

Note: This won't persist after restart unless added to config.org.

** Use-Package Syntax Reference

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  (use-package package-name
    :ensure t                      ; Install if not present
    :hook (mode-name . function)   ; Add hooks
    :bind ((\"C-c x\" . command))    ; Key bindings
    :config                        ; Run after loading
    (setq some-variable value)
    :custom                        ; Set custom variables
    (variable-name value)
    :init                          ; Run before loading
    (some-setup-function))
#+end_src

** Common Use-Package Keywords

| Keyword   | Purpose                        |
|-----------+--------------------------------|
| =:ensure= | Install package if missing     |
| =:hook=   | Add function to mode hook      |
| =:bind=   | Define keybindings             |
| =:config= | Run code after package loads   |
| =:init=   | Run code before package loads  |
| =:custom= | Set customization variables    |
| =:after=  | Load after specified package   |
| =:defer=  | Defer loading (lazy load)      |
| =:mode=   | Associate with file extensions |

** Adding System Packages (NixOS)

1. Edit =/etc/nixos/emacs-packages.nix=

2. Add packages to =environment.systemPackages=:

#+begin_src nix
  environment.systemPackages = with pkgs; [
    # ... existing packages ...
    new-package-name
  ];
#+end_src

3. Rebuild:

#+begin_src shell
  sudo nixos-rebuild switch
#+end_src

* Customization
** Changing Theme

In =config.org=, find the doom-themes section and change:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  (load-theme 'doom-one t)
#+end_src

Available themes:

- =doom-one= (dark, default)
- =doom-one-light=
- =doom-dracula=
- =doom-gruvbox=
- =doom-nord=
- =doom-solarized-dark=
- =doom-solarized-light=
- =doom-tomorrow-night=
- =doom-monokai-pro=

** Changing Fonts

In =config.org=, find the Font Configuration section. Default sizes:

| Element     | Height | Approx Size |
|-------------+--------+-------------|
| Editor text | 100    | ~10pt       |
| Modeline    | 80     | ~8pt        |
| Minibuffer  | 80     | ~8pt        |

To change the editor font:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  (set-face-attribute 'default nil
                      :font \"Fira Code\"
                      :height 120) ; 12pt
#+end_src

** Changing Hebrew Fonts

Edit the =my/latex-hebrew-preamble= variable in config.org.

Available Hebrew fonts (from culmus):

- David CLM
- Nachlieli CLM
- Miriam Mono CLM
- Frank Ruehl CLM
- Hadasim CLM

** Adding Custom Keybindings

Global keybinding:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  (global-set-key (kbd \"C-c m\") 'my-command)
#+end_src

Mode-specific:

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  (define-key org-mode-map (kbd \"C-c m\") 'my-command)
#+end_src

** Creating Custom Functions

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
  (defun my/custom-function ()
    \"Description of what this function does.\"
    (interactive)
    ;; Your code here
    (message \"Function executed!\"))

  ;; Bind to key
  (global-set-key (kbd \"C-c x\") 'my/custom-function)
#+end_src

